  "Content": {
    "Html": "<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Are you a medical professional interested in sharing resources on healthy eating with your patients or clients? To support your important efforts, we invite you to apply to receive free copies of our </span><a href=\"https://drgreger.org/collections/swag/products/healthkit\"><i><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Evidence-Based Eating Guide</span></i></a> <span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">by completing </span><a href=\"https://form.asana.com?k=0kOBgzfzCyGYZLUBLoGMmg&amp;d=69744073713181\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">this form</span></a><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">. </span></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">The </span><i><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Evidence-Based Eating Guide: A Healthy Living Resource from Dr. Greger &amp; NutritionFacts.org</span></i><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> is a tool designed to help make the switch to a healthier lifestyle even more simple. It’s easy to understand and filled with information on eating healthier, including a breakdown of</span><a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/video/dining-by-traffic-light-green-is-for-go-red-is-for-stop/\"> <span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Dr. Greger’s Traffic Light Eating</span></a><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">, tips for using his</span><a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/video/dr-gregers-daily-dozen-checklist/\"> <span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Daily Dozen checklist</span></a><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">, sample menus, and more.</span></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">We hope the guide will help you help your patients or clients improve the length and quality of their lives. (Note: This application is open to health professionals and organizations, but individuals can get the guide for free <a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/healthkit/\">here</a>.)</span></p>\n<p> </p>\n<h4><b>New Key Takeaways in Blogs </b></h4>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"><a href=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/09/NF-Blog.png/\"><img decoding=\"async\" class=\" wp-image-68739 alignleft\" src=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/09/NF-Blog-1024x1024.png\" alt=\"computer showing a nutritionfacts.org blog post\" width=\"197\" height=\"197\" srcset=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/09/NF-Blog-1024x1024.png 1024w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/09/NF-Blog-960x960.png 960w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/09/NF-Blog-768x768.png 768w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/09/NF-Blog-500x500.png 500w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/09/NF-Blog-1200x1200.png 1200w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/09/NF-Blog-720x720.png 720w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/09/NF-Blog-540x540.png 540w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/09/NF-Blog.png 2000w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 197px) 100vw, 197px\"/></a>If you’re a longtime reader of the blog, you may have noticed that they all now end with a “key takeaways” section. A summary has been a common request that I’m excited I’m now able to offer. </span><a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/subscribe/\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Sign up here</span></a><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> to have the blog delivered straight to your inbox. </span></p>\n<p> </p>\n<p> </p>\n<h4><b>Recipe: Gemelli with Zucchini Meatballs</b></h4>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"><a href=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/09/Gemelli-with-Zucchini-Meatballs-2.jpg/\"><img decoding=\"async\" class=\"size-large wp-image-68731 alignleft\" src=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/09/Gemelli-with-Zucchini-Meatballs-2-1024x1024.jpg\" alt=\"Gemelli with Zucchini Meatballs on slate background\" width=\"200\" height=\"200\" srcset=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/09/Gemelli-with-Zucchini-Meatballs-2-1024x1024.jpg 1024w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/09/Gemelli-with-Zucchini-Meatballs-2-960x960.jpg 960w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/09/Gemelli-with-Zucchini-Meatballs-2-768x768.jpg 768w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/09/Gemelli-with-Zucchini-Meatballs-2-500x500.jpg 500w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/09/Gemelli-with-Zucchini-Meatballs-2-1200x1200.jpg 1200w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/09/Gemelli-with-Zucchini-Meatballs-2-720x720.jpg 720w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/09/Gemelli-with-Zucchini-Meatballs-2-540x540.jpg 540w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 200px) 100vw, 200px\"/></a>This recipe comes from </span><a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/book/how-not-to-diet-cookbook/\"><i><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">The How Not to Diet Cookbook</span></i></a><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">. Don’t let the length intimidate you. It’s as simple to make as it is delicious. I like to make the meatballs and sauce ahead of time so their flavors develop even more. When I’m not in the mood for chimichurri sauce, I substitute my favorite salt-free marinara. Get the free recipe </span><a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/recipe/gemelli-with-zucchini-meatballs-and-avocado-chimichurri/\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">here</span></a><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">, and watch how it’s made on our </span><a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/reel/CSr0ZpOg1jz/\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Instagram</span></a><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">.</span></p>\n<p> </p>\n<p> </p>\n<h4><b>Key Takeaways: Alzheimer’s Disease</b></h4>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"><a href=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/09/KT-Alzheimers.jpg/\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" class=\"size-large wp-image-68735 alignleft\" src=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/09/KT-Alzheimers-1024x1024.jpg\" alt=\"two people holding hands\" width=\"200\" height=\"200\" srcset=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/09/KT-Alzheimers-1024x1024.jpg 1024w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/09/KT-Alzheimers-960x960.jpg 960w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/09/KT-Alzheimers-768x768.jpg 768w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/09/KT-Alzheimers-500x500.jpg 500w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/09/KT-Alzheimers-1200x1200.jpg 1200w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/09/KT-Alzheimers-720x720.jpg 720w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/09/KT-Alzheimers-540x540.jpg 540w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/09/KT-Alzheimers.jpg 2000w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 200px) 100vw, 200px\"/></a>September 21 was World Alzheimer’s Day. For me, it’s personal. My maternal grandmother died of the disease. I witnessed her decline and Alzheimer’s impact on her when I was in medical school, but my newfound knowledge was useless by then. A disease without a cure or an effective treatment, Alzheimer’s leaves millions of families devastated each year. The good news is that it may be preventable. Read more, and check out all of my videos on the subject on the </span><a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/topics/alzheimers-disease//\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">topic page</span></a><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">.</span></p>\n<p> </p>\n<h4><b>Seeking Graphic Design Volunteer</b></h4>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"><a href=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/09/hands-III.png/\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" class=\" wp-image-68733 alignleft\" src=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/09/hands-III.png\" alt=\"four illustrated hands\" width=\"200\" height=\"190\"/></a>We are seeking a Volunteer Production Assistant to regularly support our Design Director with the creation of banner ads and original thumbnails for </span><a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">NutritionFacts.org</span></a><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">’s YouTube videos. For more information and to apply, please go to our </span><a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/volunteer/\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">volunteer page</span></a><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">.</span></p>\n<p> </p>\n<p> </p>\n<p> </p>\n<h4><b>Volunteer Spotlight: Tamara Amor </b></h4>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"><a href=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/09/Screen-Shot-2021-09-15-at-5.02.42-PM-e1631821098510.png/\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" class=\"wp-image-68743  alignleft\" src=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/09/Screen-Shot-2021-09-15-at-5.02.42-PM-e1631821098510.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"200\" height=\"200\" srcset=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/09/Screen-Shot-2021-09-15-at-5.02.42-PM-e1631821098510.png 886w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/09/Screen-Shot-2021-09-15-at-5.02.42-PM-e1631821098510-768x768.png 768w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/09/Screen-Shot-2021-09-15-at-5.02.42-PM-e1631821098510-500x500.png 500w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/09/Screen-Shot-2021-09-15-at-5.02.42-PM-e1631821098510-720x720.png 720w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/09/Screen-Shot-2021-09-15-at-5.02.42-PM-e1631821098510-540x540.png 540w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 200px) 100vw, 200px\"/></a>“I started volunteering at NutritionFacts.org as a translator almost two years ago. I have been following a WFPB diet for four years now, but I have always been fond of nutrition and research. I am constantly looking for the best ways to nourish our body and be environmentally friendly at the same time, so I thought that being part of this beautiful team was a great opportunity to keep doing it.</span></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">I’m a really savoury person, so I would say that my favourite WFPB recipe is any BIG salad with legumes, roasted veggies, and quinoa or rice. I could eat that every day, especially if it has a tahini dressing or hummus in it!”</span></p>\n<p> </p>\n<h4 style=\"text-align: center;\"><a href=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2019/08/Top-3-Videos-of-the-Month.png/\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" class=\"alignnone size-large wp-image-60211\" src=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2019/08/Top-3-Videos-of-the-Month-1024x331.png\" alt=\"Top 3 Videos of the Month\" width=\"460\" height=\"149\" srcset=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2019/08/Top-3-Videos-of-the-Month-1024x331.png 1024w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2019/08/Top-3-Videos-of-the-Month-960x310.png 960w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2019/08/Top-3-Videos-of-the-Month-768x248.png 768w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2019/08/Top-3-Videos-of-the-Month-720x233.png 720w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2019/08/Top-3-Videos-of-the-Month-540x174.png 540w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2019/08/Top-3-Videos-of-the-Month.png 1108w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 460px) 100vw, 460px\"/></a></h4>\n<p> </p>\n<p><a href=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/07/54-19-Fruits-and-Vegetables-Put-to-the-Test-for-Boosting-Mood.jpg/\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" class=\" wp-image-68077 alignleft\" src=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/07/54-19-Fruits-and-Vegetables-Put-to-the-Test-for-Boosting-Mood-1024x576.jpg\" alt=\"Fruits and Vegetables Put to the Test for Boosting Mood\" width=\"201\" height=\"113\" srcset=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/07/54-19-Fruits-and-Vegetables-Put-to-the-Test-for-Boosting-Mood-1024x576.jpg 1024w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/07/54-19-Fruits-and-Vegetables-Put-to-the-Test-for-Boosting-Mood-960x540.jpg 960w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/07/54-19-Fruits-and-Vegetables-Put-to-the-Test-for-Boosting-Mood-768x432.jpg 768w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/07/54-19-Fruits-and-Vegetables-Put-to-the-Test-for-Boosting-Mood-480x270.jpg 480w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/07/54-19-Fruits-and-Vegetables-Put-to-the-Test-for-Boosting-Mood-1200x675.jpg 1200w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/07/54-19-Fruits-and-Vegetables-Put-to-the-Test-for-Boosting-Mood-720x405.jpg 720w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/07/54-19-Fruits-and-Vegetables-Put-to-the-Test-for-Boosting-Mood-540x304.jpg 540w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/07/54-19-Fruits-and-Vegetables-Put-to-the-Test-for-Boosting-Mood.jpg 1920w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 201px) 100vw, 201px\"/></a></p>\n<p><a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/video/fruits-and-vegetables-put-to-the-test-for-boosting-mood/\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Fruits and Vegetables Put to the Test for Boosting Mood</span></a><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">: A randomized controlled trial investigates diet and psychological well-being.</span></p>\n<p> </p>\n<p> </p>\n<p> </p>\n<p><a href=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/07/54-18-Exploiting-Sensory-Specific-Satiety-for-Weight-Loss.jpg/\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" class=\" wp-image-68071 alignleft\" src=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/07/54-18-Exploiting-Sensory-Specific-Satiety-for-Weight-Loss-1024x576.jpg\" alt=\"Exploiting Sensory-Specific Satiety for Weight Loss\" width=\"198\" height=\"111\" srcset=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/07/54-18-Exploiting-Sensory-Specific-Satiety-for-Weight-Loss-1024x576.jpg 1024w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/07/54-18-Exploiting-Sensory-Specific-Satiety-for-Weight-Loss-960x540.jpg 960w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/07/54-18-Exploiting-Sensory-Specific-Satiety-for-Weight-Loss-768x432.jpg 768w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/07/54-18-Exploiting-Sensory-Specific-Satiety-for-Weight-Loss-480x270.jpg 480w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/07/54-18-Exploiting-Sensory-Specific-Satiety-for-Weight-Loss-1200x675.jpg 1200w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/07/54-18-Exploiting-Sensory-Specific-Satiety-for-Weight-Loss-720x405.jpg 720w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/07/54-18-Exploiting-Sensory-Specific-Satiety-for-Weight-Loss-540x304.jpg 540w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/07/54-18-Exploiting-Sensory-Specific-Satiety-for-Weight-Loss.jpg 1920w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 198px) 100vw, 198px\"/></a><a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/video/exploiting-sensory-specific-satiety-for-weight-loss/\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Exploiting Sensory-Specific Satiety for Weight Loss</span></a><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">: How can we use sensory-specific satiety to our advantage?</span></p>\n<p> </p>\n<p> </p>\n<p> </p>\n<p><a href=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/07/54-22-How-Much-Do-Doctors-Actually-Know-About-Nutrition.jpg/\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" class=\" wp-image-68131 alignleft\" src=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/07/54-22-How-Much-Do-Doctors-Actually-Know-About-Nutrition-1024x576.jpg\" alt=\"How Much Do Doctors Actually Know About Nutrition?\" width=\"201\" height=\"113\" srcset=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/07/54-22-How-Much-Do-Doctors-Actually-Know-About-Nutrition-1024x576.jpg 1024w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/07/54-22-How-Much-Do-Doctors-Actually-Know-About-Nutrition-960x540.jpg 960w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/07/54-22-How-Much-Do-Doctors-Actually-Know-About-Nutrition-768x432.jpg 768w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/07/54-22-How-Much-Do-Doctors-Actually-Know-About-Nutrition-480x270.jpg 480w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/07/54-22-How-Much-Do-Doctors-Actually-Know-About-Nutrition-1200x675.jpg 1200w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/07/54-22-How-Much-Do-Doctors-Actually-Know-About-Nutrition-720x405.jpg 720w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/07/54-22-How-Much-Do-Doctors-Actually-Know-About-Nutrition-540x304.jpg 540w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/07/54-22-How-Much-Do-Doctors-Actually-Know-About-Nutrition.jpg 1920w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 201px) 100vw, 201px\"/></a><a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/video/how-much-do-doctors-actually-know-about-nutrition/\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">How Much Do Doctors Actually Know About Nutrition?</span></a><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">: See if you know more about basic nutrition than most doctors.</span></p>\n<p> </p>\n<h2> </h2>\n<h2> </h2>\n<h4><b>Live Q&amp;A Today </b></h4>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"><a href=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/09/Live.jpg/\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" class=\"size-large wp-image-68737 alignleft\" src=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/09/Live-1024x1024.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"200\" height=\"200\" srcset=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/09/Live-1024x1024.jpg 1024w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/09/Live-960x960.jpg 960w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/09/Live-768x768.jpg 768w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/09/Live-500x500.jpg 500w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/09/Live-1200x1200.jpg 1200w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/09/Live-720x720.jpg 720w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/09/Live-540x540.jpg 540w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2021/09/Live.jpg 2000w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 200px) 100vw, 200px\"/></a>Every other month, I do a Q&amp;A live from my treadmill, and it’s happening today!</span></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Join on our </span><a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/NutritionFacts.org/\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Facebook</span></a><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> page or </span><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/c/NutritionfactsOrgMD/live\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">YouTube</span></a><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> channel at 3pm EDT. I’ll be streaming to both at the same time!</span></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">You can find links to past live Q&amp;As </span><a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/live/\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">here</span></a><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> on NutritionFacts.org. If that’s not enough, remember, I have an </span><a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/audio/\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">audio podcast</span></a><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> to keep you company, too. </span></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">P.S. I recently chatted with my friend, Chef AJ. You can find that conversation </span><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=tw3bqkzagK8\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">here</span></a><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">. And you can now follow us on <a href=\"https://www.tiktok.com/@nutrition_facts_org\">TikTok</a>.</span></p>\n<p> </p>\n<p>In health,<br/>\n<b>Michael Greger, M.D.</b></p>\n<p>PS: If you haven’t yet, you can subscribe to my free videos <a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/subscribe/\"><b>here</b></a><b> </b>and watch my live, year-in-review presentations:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>2019: <a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/video/evidence-based-weight-loss-live-presentation/\"><b>Evidence-Based Weight Loss</b></a></li>\n<li>2016: <a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/video/how-not-to-die/\"><b>How Not To Die: The Role of Diet in Preventing, Arresting, and Reversing Our Top 15 Killers</b></a></li>\n<li>2015: <a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/video/food-as-medicine/\"><b>Food as Medicine: Preventing and Treating the Most Dreaded Diseases with Diet</b></a></li>\n<li>2014: <a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/video/from-table-to-able/\"><b>From Table to Able: Combating Disabling Diseases with Food</b></a></li>\n<li>2013: <a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/video/more-than-an-apple-a-day-preventing-our-most-common-diseases/\"><b>More Than an Apple a Day</b></a></li>\n<li>2012: <a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/video/uprooting-the-leading-causes-of-death/\"><b>Uprooting the Leading Causes of Death</b></a></li>\n</ul>"
